==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|svá|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|swa|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|swe|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|swe|lang=ine-pro}} and {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|se|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old English {{term|swa|swā|lang=ang}} (English {{term|so|lang=en}}), Old Frisian {{term|sa|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|so|sō|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|zo|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|so|sō|lang=goh}} (German {{term|so|lang=de}}), Swedish {{term|så|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|så|lang=da}}, Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍅𐌰|lang=got}}, Latin {{term|si|lang=la}} (from an earlier form {{term|suad|lang=la}}), Oscan {{term|svai|svaí}}, Umbrian {{term|sve}}, Greek {{term|ὡς}} (earlier '''*ϝος''').

